{"name":"Broad Daylight","hex":"#bbddff","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"broad daylight","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Abundant natural illumination in daytime, producing clear visibility; hence, daytime.","Chiefly preceded by in: the full view of observers during the day."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/broad_daylight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Broad Daylight (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Broad Daylight is a 1922 American silent crime film directed by Irving Cummings and written by Harvey Gates. The film stars Lois Wilson, Jack Mulhall, Ralph Lewis, Kenneth Gibson, Wilton Taylor, and Ben Hewlett. The film was released on October 30, 1922, by Universal Film Manufacturing Company."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Broad_Daylight_lobby_card.jpg/330px-Broad_Daylight_lobby_card.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Broad_Daylight_(film)","wikidata":"Q3645158"},{"title":"Daylight","blocks":[{"text":"Daylight is the combination of all direct and indirect sunlight during the daytime. This includes direct sunlight, diffuse sky radiation, and (often) both of these reflected by Earth and terrestrial objects, like landforms and buildings. Sunlight scattered or reflected by astronomical objects is generally not considered daylight. Therefore, daylight excludes moonlight, despite it being reflected indirect sunlight."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Daylight.png/330px-Daylight.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daylight","wikidata":"Q16491"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Broad_Daylight_lobby_card.jpg/500px-Broad_Daylight_lobby_card.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/